# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      (macOS/Linux)
#   copy .env.example .env    (Windows)
#
# Ask Sang You for the actual Supabase credentials — they are NOT in this repo
# and must never be committed. `.env` is gitignored; keep it that way.
#
# You can also find these in the Supabase dashboard:
#   Project Settings → API → Project URL + anon/publishable key

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# NOTE: there is deliberately no GEMINI_API_KEY here any more.
#
# Everything in this file ships inside the app bundle — `.env` is a Flutter
# asset, so `unzip app-release.apk && cat assets/flutter_assets/.env` reveals
# it verbatim. That is acceptable for the Supabase URL and anon key (the anon
# key is designed to be public and every request is still gated by RLS), but
# not for a billable Gemini credential.
#
# The Gemini key now lives server-side as a Supabase secret, used only by the
# `gemini-proxy` Edge Function:
#
#   npx supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# See docs/GEMINI_PROXY_SETUP.md. With no backend configured the app falls back
# to the built-in offline mock AI services, exactly as it did before.

# No map API key needed - map tiles and place search both run on
# OpenStreetMap (see docs/MAP_LOCATION_SETUP.md and docs/PLACES_SEARCH_SETUP.md).
